                <pb facs="0300" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./54: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-23T19:00:00-03:00">February 23, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 23—5:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Your 13, February 21. Guani tells me that he cabled an affirmative reply
                    yesterday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
